# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Restricted data — must never be committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The crash panel is derived from Lebanese Red Cross ambulance dispatch
# records and CNRS-L tari2ak GPS data. Neither provider has authorised public
# release, and the panel carries per-cell patient detail (n_status_dead,
# n_female / n_male, mean_age, cause breakdowns) well beyond the aggregate
# figures the paper reports. The manuscript's Data Availability section states
# that these datasets are not publicly available, so the repository must stay
# consistent with that.
#
# Derived products that aggregate to the published level are fine to commit:
# src/partitioning/data/risk-table.json and sandbox/ccr/risk-table-corrected.json
# hold only the 7 regions x 5 slots fitted rates.
data/panel/

# Per-cell observed crash counts. predictions.csv carries n_crashes for each
# region x month x time-slot cell of the holdout window (350 cells, 412
# crashes). That is finer than anything the paper reports, and it is the
# restricted panel's response variable, so it stays local. The aggregate
# scores derived from it -- comparison.csv and comparison.json -- are
# published instead, and anyone with authorised access to the panel can
# regenerate predictions.csv with scripts/validation/step2_fit_predict.py.
data/validation/predictions.csv
